Changes from upstream:

- OpenID Connect single sign-on: optional sign-in through one or more
  OIDC providers, with an entitlement policy, a `pushed` policy and an
  OIDC-only mode. See docs/oidc-sso.md.
- Tenancy push: PUT/GET /tenancy, which provisions one Account and Project
  per shop from the platform's push and decides who may sign in through
  the `pushed` provider. See docs/oidc-sso.md.
- Build and CI: a nix/devenv development environment with a local kanidm
  identity provider, and the deployed container image, both built by
  flake.nix (packages.<linux>.image, nix/image.nix); a CI workflow
  (.gitea/workflows/) builds and publishes that image. ops/Dockerfile is
  upstream's and is not the deployed build.
- Secrets from files: SECRET_KEY_BASE, KEILA_PASSWORD, DB_PASSWORD,
  MAILER_SMTP_PASSWORD, CAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY, HASHID_SALT and the OIDC client
  secrets can each be read from the file named by <NAME>_FILE.
- Source link: every page of the web interface links the source code of
  the running version (KEILA_SOURCE_URL, KEILA_SOURCE_REVISION), as
  required by section 13 of the AGPL.

The extra/ directory is upstream's Keila Cloud code. It is not licensed
under the AGPL (see extra/README.md), is left untouched by this fork and
is not compiled into its builds.
